  "implementation": [
    "Explicit NativeDtmfGatewayOrigin distinguishes initial and established SIP origins. Each typed variant uses its own current independent named signal pair reader; no deserializable origin or native/initial surrogate is manufactured.",
    "Schema102 binds established recipients to actual telephone_connection_lifetimes and committed descriptor call/runtime/generation/route identity. The shared deliveries view preserves atomic mixed-batch capacity, recipient ceilings, one original reservation, aggregation and successor recovery. Established rows are immutable and included in logical snapshot digests.",
    "Runtime discovers the actual committed replacement policy/controller and one immutable registration. Each write matches its original origin and exact replacement incarnation, reacquires current source dtmf.send and destination route dtmf.receive under one authority interval, and holds the original/current Core audience and physical fence. Signal reads never create RTP grants.",
    "Committed lifetime discovery uses the actual established active owner, runtime and physical context. The disposable preparation worker and its immutable Preparing binding snapshot cannot be used as ongoing Active-call requirements.",
    "The shared SIP fixture checks an actual pending reserved SIP schedule in native_dtmf_deliveries before acknowledging INFO, covering both initial and established rows without dropping the existing call/method/state checks.",
    "HTTP operation schema remains unchanged. The generated server reference and developer guide describe established recipient authority, original schedules and the remaining moved-call received-source work."
  ],
